WEBVTT

00:13.888 --> 00:18.393
Those who ceaselessly hone
their killing arts are known as "Masters."

00:18.810 --> 00:23.815
After many generations,
they have gained lethal abilities

00:23.898 --> 00:26.359
called "Modified Bloodlines."

00:27.068 --> 00:32.365
This is the story of one such Master,
the Poison Master, Hikaru Gero,

00:32.657 --> 00:35.326
and his attempts to get married.

00:43.793 --> 00:47.255
Locked in Latata

00:47.338 --> 00:50.925
Secrets in my veins Latata

00:51.009 --> 00:52.719
I know you want it

00:52.802 --> 00:54.512
And sure, I love it

00:54.596 --> 00:58.767
So I stay behind the mask Latata

00:58.850 --> 01:02.103
Run, run, run back to back Run

01:02.187 --> 01:05.982
Fun, fun, fun unpredictable but fun

01:06.066 --> 01:08.193
At the end of every mind game

01:08.276 --> 01:12.155
Shoot through the darkened night

01:12.238 --> 01:15.366
Poisoned in our bodies still

01:15.450 --> 01:20.038
Laugh at us our reckless souls

01:20.121 --> 01:21.372
TOXIC

01:21.456 --> 01:23.666
For you I will

01:23.750 --> 01:24.959
TOXIC

01:25.043 --> 01:27.378
Rewrite my destiny

01:27.462 --> 01:30.882
Losing it, falling for you

01:30.965 --> 01:34.344
What's tomorrow Kill or Kiss

01:34.427 --> 01:35.553
TOXIC

01:35.637 --> 01:37.889
Tell me what you want

01:37.972 --> 01:39.140
TOXIC

01:39.224 --> 01:41.434
I'll stay right here

01:41.518 --> 01:44.896
Like a spell, I'll be by your side

01:44.979 --> 01:48.650
What you gonna do Kill or Kiss

01:52.570 --> 01:55.156
Kill or Kiss

01:56.241 --> 01:58.701
Kill or Kiss

01:59.786 --> 02:02.038
Kill or Kiss

02:07.502 --> 02:09.420
Cheers!

02:16.719 --> 02:18.805
Okay, thanks for waiting!

02:18.888 --> 02:20.723
Here's your lemon sours.

02:22.559 --> 02:24.894
I hope Gero's up to this.

02:27.897 --> 02:30.942
So this is a college welcome party?
I've heard the legends.

02:32.235 --> 02:34.612
I never thought my job
would take me to one.

02:34.696 --> 02:36.614
New students, gather round.

02:36.698 --> 02:38.241
Coming.

02:42.245 --> 02:45.707
Okay. To all of us starting college
and meeting each other.

02:45.790 --> 02:46.708
Cheers!

02:46.791 --> 02:48.710
Cheers!

02:53.256 --> 02:55.174
You're a first-year, right?

02:56.718 --> 02:58.803
How's the party? Having fun?

03:01.055 --> 03:05.143
Huh? Uh... Huh?

03:10.481 --> 03:14.736
I'm h-having a blast.

03:14.819 --> 03:15.612
What did I do?

03:15.945 --> 03:17.363
Whatever we did, sorry.

03:17.447 --> 03:19.073
S-See you around.

03:23.536 --> 03:26.623
That was my chance to talk
with older students, and I blew it.

03:29.834 --> 03:34.714
I want to hire you as a bodyguard for my
niece, who starts university this spring.

03:35.340 --> 03:40.929
But if possible, without standing out.

03:41.471 --> 03:43.514
I'm Shiori Ureshino.

03:43.973 --> 03:46.809
Her father, my older brother,

03:46.893 --> 03:50.271
built this company from the ground up
in one generation,

03:50.605 --> 03:53.316
but illness took him a year ago.

03:53.566 --> 03:56.945
He left a will
stating his daughter, Shiori,

03:57.028 --> 04:01.282
will succeed him as CEO
once she comes of age.

04:01.866 --> 04:06.704
But someone has other ideas.

04:07.372 --> 04:09.249
My older sister.

04:09.832 --> 04:13.336
She claims Balzak is rightfully hers.

04:13.836 --> 04:16.714
I don't exactly know what Futae will try,

04:17.090 --> 04:20.927
but rumor has it she's hired someone
who uses strange techniques

04:21.010 --> 04:24.639
that no ordinary expert
has a hope of stopping.

04:25.515 --> 04:30.770
Um, thank you very much
for taking this job.

04:31.729 --> 04:33.773
That's your student ID.

04:34.107 --> 04:37.193
Starting today, you're Daigo Oshima,
a third-year student.

04:37.277 --> 04:38.361
Seriously?

04:38.695 --> 04:39.946
E-Excuse me.

04:40.780 --> 04:47.287
I know this is, uh, sudden,
but I'd like to, well...

04:47.996 --> 04:50.331
go to a drinking party.

04:50.665 --> 04:53.084
A party? That's a risk you don't need.

04:54.043 --> 04:55.336
Please.

05:00.842 --> 05:03.052
O-Oh, all right.

05:07.390 --> 05:09.142
Okay, next person.

05:10.143 --> 05:16.107
I-I'm Shiori Ureshino,
a first-year economics major.

05:17.233 --> 05:20.528
A-And, uh...

05:26.868 --> 05:29.871
What should I say now?

05:45.928 --> 05:48.306
P-Pleased to meet you all.

05:49.766 --> 05:53.227
Huh? Uh, thanks.

05:53.478 --> 05:55.354
Okay, next person.

05:59.817 --> 06:01.778
Can you handle a party, Gero?

06:01.861 --> 06:04.530
I've gone drinking with
the Bug Master plenty of times.

06:05.907 --> 06:08.367
I'm worried. I'd better sneak in.

06:09.118 --> 06:14.624
I'll show you that a top-notch Master
is also the life of the party.

06:15.917 --> 06:18.252
Daigo Oshima, economics major.

06:19.128 --> 06:21.714
Watch as I chug all eight of these.

06:25.426 --> 06:27.136
There's no way that flies these days.

06:33.017 --> 06:34.894
This next part is the clincher.

06:42.610 --> 06:44.278
Should we call an ambulance?

06:59.752 --> 07:01.754
That'll get applause for sure.

07:03.297 --> 07:04.465
It's nice to meet you.

07:06.384 --> 07:10.388
I-It's a water-absorbent polymer.
Completely harmless.

07:10.471 --> 07:11.889
What a disaster.

07:13.474 --> 07:16.018
Okay, who else hasn't
introduced themselves?

07:16.102 --> 07:17.687
Hey, he's calling you.

07:20.189 --> 07:21.190
(Ultimate Relaxation, Man of the Alps)
(Campfire ASMR)

07:31.492 --> 07:32.910
I'm Naruko.

07:34.871 --> 07:35.788
That's all.

07:36.581 --> 07:39.709
Uh, what about first name?
Your major? Stuff like that?

07:39.792 --> 07:41.002
I forget.

07:42.670 --> 07:49.260
What really matters is that I got to meet
all of you here in this moment.

07:49.886 --> 07:51.929
I super thank my lucky stars.

07:52.013 --> 07:53.347
What's his deal?

07:53.431 --> 07:55.349
He's been spacing out this whole time.

07:57.018 --> 07:58.019
I super thank them.

07:59.729 --> 08:00.938
He barely said anything.

08:01.022 --> 08:02.523
Why'd he say it twice?

08:02.982 --> 08:05.193
He's the one for me.

08:07.361 --> 08:09.489
Naruko, is this seat taken?

08:09.572 --> 08:12.241
Wish I got the benefit
of the doubt like that.

08:12.325 --> 08:14.118
It's gotta be his looks.

08:15.328 --> 08:18.623
Drinking parties have hidden depths.

08:22.418 --> 08:24.253
Aw, paid by the hour.

08:25.671 --> 08:27.507
Listen, Ureshino.

08:28.382 --> 08:29.383
I'm so sorry.

08:29.634 --> 08:33.304
Don't make her cry, Gero.
Did you take your screwup out on her?

08:33.387 --> 08:35.640
No, I didn't say anything about that.

08:38.184 --> 08:40.811
But I mean, why did you
force yourself to go?

08:41.312 --> 08:45.316
You're inheriting a company, so you went
to work on your communication issues.

08:45.399 --> 08:47.818
I get that, but even so...

08:50.738 --> 08:52.156
H-Hey now.

08:52.240 --> 08:53.824
Really, Gero?

08:55.034 --> 09:01.207
No, I'm just so glad you're thinking
about how I feel.

09:02.500 --> 09:06.087
But, well, it's not just
about the company.

09:06.420 --> 09:10.508
I want to be part of the group.

09:13.928 --> 09:16.973
At the very end, my dad said...

09:21.435 --> 09:26.315
Give drinking a try when you turn 20.

09:30.069 --> 09:34.198
Shiori, you're a nice girl,

09:34.782 --> 09:37.618
but you worry too much
about what other people think.

09:37.952 --> 09:42.415
Life's more fun when you take
what's rattling around inside your head

09:42.498 --> 09:46.377
and bam! You let it all out.

09:46.711 --> 09:51.257
Enjoy yourself with people.

09:51.966 --> 09:55.761
That's what I want for you.

10:07.690 --> 10:09.191
I can't do it.

10:09.525 --> 10:14.947
Even here, a flood of words
sometimes just overwhelms my brain.

10:15.615 --> 10:16.991
Ureshino.

10:17.074 --> 10:21.287
I know. I just need
to take the first step.

10:21.912 --> 10:24.832
Everyone will accept me.

10:25.166 --> 10:27.627
My brain knows that,
but I can't help worrying.

10:27.710 --> 10:33.883
What if I make people annoyed
or angry or sad instead?

10:35.635 --> 10:39.930
I never even managed to really talk
to my dad before he...

10:40.640 --> 10:45.102
I didn't even get to ask why
he named me his successor.

10:47.938 --> 10:49.106
So...

10:49.440 --> 10:51.734
I want to improve myself.

10:52.193 --> 10:54.070
To get to the point...

10:54.945 --> 10:58.366
where I can laugh away my fear.

10:59.992 --> 11:02.703
You realize someone's
out to kill you, right?

11:03.496 --> 11:04.747
Gero.

11:06.123 --> 11:08.959
But if you've got someplace
you want to go, I won't stop you.

11:11.212 --> 11:14.382
My job is to keep you safe.

11:19.053 --> 11:21.847
Madam, I have something to report.

11:22.681 --> 11:24.725
Her bodyguard is good.

11:25.309 --> 11:29.814
He acts all natural,
but he leaves no openings.

11:35.986 --> 11:38.697
I super forgot to charge it.

11:41.158 --> 11:43.077
(The Sound Master)

11:44.161 --> 11:45.204
You think this is funny?

11:45.287 --> 11:48.082
You've been at this for a month
and made zero progress.

11:48.165 --> 11:50.709
Do you realize how much I'm paying you?

11:50.793 --> 11:54.797
As if that little girl could run
a party supplies brand

11:54.880 --> 11:57.967
with a market cap of 1.5 trillion yen.

11:58.050 --> 12:00.970
Tell me: When do you plan
to "dispose" of her?

12:03.848 --> 12:05.850
The time is not yet ripe.

12:05.933 --> 12:08.894
Excuse me? Don't give me that crap.

12:08.978 --> 12:10.688
I've spent over a month-

12:18.737 --> 12:20.698
This bodyguard, Oshima.

12:21.031 --> 12:23.993
You say he's good,
but he's still a nobody.

12:24.076 --> 12:27.121
He won't last a second
against a Master like you.

12:27.538 --> 12:31.041
Madam, I'm super a man of my word.

12:31.750 --> 12:33.377
In any case...

12:33.461 --> 12:36.714
Either get her to decline the job,

12:37.256 --> 12:40.092
or leave her incapable of taking it.

12:40.509 --> 12:44.638
You can kill her if that's what it takes.

12:48.684 --> 12:53.439
Gero, you're not a real student.
Why even bother to listen so attentively?

12:53.522 --> 12:56.525
This is all new to me.
I'm having a great time.

12:56.817 --> 12:59.278
You've got one hell of a tragic past.

13:00.237 --> 13:01.197
Tomorrow.

13:01.739 --> 13:03.365
Okay, you there.

13:03.449 --> 13:05.910
Name a product that
revolutionized its industry.

13:05.993 --> 13:07.495
Huh? Uh...

13:07.995 --> 13:09.538
Mixy-Mix Max Mix.

13:09.788 --> 13:14.877
Only 100 of these legendary kits were made
for the brand's 30th anniversary.

13:15.252 --> 13:18.672
Well, well. You know your stuff.

13:46.158 --> 13:48.369
Liberating the Mixy-Mix market!

13:48.452 --> 13:50.246
A return to the Mix-aissance!

13:50.329 --> 13:52.248
In other words, Mixy-Mix...

13:52.581 --> 13:53.457
Max Mix!

13:55.084 --> 13:57.753
As long as there are
passionate students like you,

13:57.836 --> 14:00.005
I can make way for
the next generation without-

14:05.094 --> 14:06.011
It looks like...

14:06.345 --> 14:10.516
since they can't separate me from
the target, they're using brute force.

14:11.433 --> 14:12.977
Who here seems suspicious?

14:16.564 --> 14:17.606
Someone outside?

14:17.856 --> 14:22.278
But I already checked that
no one had a line of sight.

14:41.338 --> 14:43.716
We were attacked all at once.

14:44.091 --> 14:47.511
However, this is a
well-ventilated environment.

14:48.345 --> 14:50.306
That means it wasn't a gas.

14:50.890 --> 14:52.182
In which case...

14:53.142 --> 14:56.896
He injected himself with something,
then sprang into action.

14:57.354 --> 15:01.650
Were sound waves transmitted remotely
to shake the room and the people inside?

15:01.901 --> 15:05.946
I scrambled his sense of balance,
and he super recovered in no time.

15:06.030 --> 15:07.656
That should be impossible.

15:07.907 --> 15:11.493
No one could pull off a precise,
large-scale attack except...

15:11.577 --> 15:15.664
No one could whip something
like that up in an instant except...

15:16.749 --> 15:18.042
- ...a Sound Master.
- ...a Poison Master.

15:22.546 --> 15:23.505
Gero!

15:24.506 --> 15:26.550
I informed the client.

15:26.634 --> 15:31.597
Every hitman knows that making it look
like an accident saves trouble.

15:31.972 --> 15:35.893
Ureshino, they planned
to kill you for sure.

15:37.227 --> 15:41.023
So, Gero, should we skip
the camping trip tomorrow?

15:41.106 --> 15:42.942
That's up to our client.

15:44.151 --> 15:46.070
Of course you can go.

15:46.779 --> 15:48.364
I-I can?

15:48.447 --> 15:52.493
You've been looking forward
to this trip for ages.

15:53.118 --> 15:57.164
There's no substitute for friends
you make at school.

15:57.498 --> 15:59.583
So go make lots of them.

15:59.667 --> 16:03.128
With those two around,
you have nothing to worry about.

16:04.880 --> 16:06.298
Morning.

16:06.382 --> 16:09.051
See you, Uncle Mitsuhiko.

16:09.718 --> 16:11.887
Sorry for keeping you waiting.

16:11.971 --> 16:15.891
It's no problem. That's a huge bag,
though. What's in it?

16:18.018 --> 16:19.853
Have a safe trip.

16:26.360 --> 16:29.571
We can't guarantee her safety
even if she stays home.

16:30.489 --> 16:33.659
The only way to resolve this
is to face the enemy.

16:34.994 --> 16:39.999
And unlike with Himekawa, we don't know
when the Sound Master will strike.

16:41.083 --> 16:43.085
Is the plan to settle things
on this trip?

16:49.216 --> 16:50.259
Hey, what's this?

16:50.342 --> 16:51.969
(1 more day)
Hey, what's this?

16:52.052 --> 16:54.513
A super important promise.

16:54.596 --> 16:56.098
You're such a great guy, Naruko.

16:56.181 --> 16:58.058
I'll make a promise, too.

16:58.308 --> 17:01.353
Oh? Then, make a promise with me, too.

17:02.312 --> 17:04.148
Super important.

17:22.291 --> 17:27.921
A man who can cook attracts triple
the ladies (Kinosaki approved).

17:30.924 --> 17:33.343
I'll show you I can cook
with the best of them.

17:34.219 --> 17:38.474
Um, would you like some yakisoba?

17:40.476 --> 17:43.729
Would anyone, uh, like some yakisoba?

17:44.730 --> 17:46.565
Yakisoba?

17:48.025 --> 17:49.443
Hey, Kinosaki.

17:49.526 --> 17:51.612
"Don't worry about me."

17:52.863 --> 17:55.491
That's what Ureshino told us, remember?

17:56.241 --> 17:59.661
She wants to "figure it out" for herself.

18:04.458 --> 18:07.961
How do I become part of the group?

18:18.555 --> 18:19.765
Is she okay?

18:24.603 --> 18:26.814
If talking to people doesn't work...

18:27.481 --> 18:29.066
I'll try something else.

18:30.442 --> 18:32.444
What's with the magical girl getup?

18:38.367 --> 18:40.494
Nothing up my sleeves.

18:41.537 --> 18:42.746
And here goes nothing.

18:43.372 --> 18:46.041
Pan-puru pin-puru pom-po-pun.

18:46.125 --> 18:48.919
Pin-puru pan-puru pom-po-pun.

18:49.002 --> 18:50.754
Whoa!

18:55.092 --> 18:57.386
For my next trick, an extra big helping.

18:57.636 --> 19:00.597
Pin-puru pan-puru pom-po-pun!

19:00.681 --> 19:01.557
Huh?

19:04.351 --> 19:06.103
You okay?

19:10.274 --> 19:13.068
Those were some cool
magic tricks, Ureshino.

19:13.694 --> 19:16.405
I got them from my family's business.

19:17.197 --> 19:21.994
I've never done that in front of people
before, and I messed up the finale.

19:22.703 --> 19:25.414
I'm not good with words...

19:26.540 --> 19:31.670
But I remembered the performance
Mr. Gero put on at the party,

19:31.753 --> 19:33.255
and I thought "That's it!"

19:35.424 --> 19:36.884
Thank you very much.

19:41.138 --> 19:42.598
I didn't really, um...

19:44.433 --> 19:45.309
I mean...

19:46.852 --> 19:48.562
You're welcome.

19:49.354 --> 19:51.481
That reminds me. Have you all heard...

19:52.733 --> 19:55.402
about the curse of Lord Chladni?

19:55.485 --> 19:57.070
Huh? What's that?

19:58.030 --> 20:00.032
This used to be a village.

20:00.365 --> 20:04.328
The locals made "offerings" to the local
deity right up until World War II.

20:05.245 --> 20:08.248
Once every two years,
when the crops failed,

20:08.624 --> 20:12.878
they would pick out
the youngest child in the village,

20:13.921 --> 20:18.342
and lock the child up
in that shrine there.

20:43.116 --> 20:46.119
They abandoned the custom after the war,

20:46.787 --> 20:49.957
but landslides, fires, and a bunch
of other disasters followed.

20:50.290 --> 20:53.627
And although nearly a thousand people
lived here at its peak,

20:53.710 --> 20:56.421
it wasn't long before not a soul remained.

20:59.174 --> 21:04.346
But even now, Lord Chladni
waits for his next offering.

21:04.972 --> 21:06.765
And that is...

21:06.848 --> 21:09.184
you!

21:09.268 --> 21:10.352
He made all that up.

21:10.602 --> 21:14.815
Oshima, no one likes a spoilsport.

21:14.898 --> 21:17.693
Sorry, Ureshino. It's all true.

21:19.194 --> 21:21.154
I think that's enough buildup.

21:21.238 --> 21:21.989
Yup.

21:23.031 --> 21:25.158
Now, let's get this party started.

21:25.617 --> 21:28.370
It's the moment you've all been
waiting for: the test of courage.

21:28.453 --> 21:29.621
Wait, for real?

21:29.705 --> 21:31.039
Oh, come on.

21:31.123 --> 21:33.041
Hey, have you seen Naruko?

21:33.292 --> 21:35.544
I'd love to pair up with him.

21:57.524 --> 22:01.820
The melody of this forest
is super perfect.

22:03.864 --> 22:06.116
Shiori Ureshino.

22:06.575 --> 22:09.995
My killer session with your screams...

22:14.291 --> 22:15.667
...begins now.

22:28.722 --> 22:30.932
Ah! Something smells fishy!

22:31.016 --> 22:32.851
I'm shocked, startled,
it's adding insult to injury

22:32.934 --> 22:34.186
I'm completely obsessed

22:34.269 --> 22:36.563
Ah! Something smells off!

22:36.646 --> 22:38.565
You're all bluff,
I'm sick and tired, so disappointed

22:38.648 --> 22:39.691
Bye-bye, mwah!

22:39.983 --> 22:42.736
It seems like I'm only good at

22:42.819 --> 22:45.572
workbooks for a child

22:45.655 --> 22:48.325
Even through infectious disease,
I want to love with you

22:48.408 --> 22:51.286
No! No! Love's in gridlock!

22:51.369 --> 22:53.789
Forever and ever, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

22:53.872 --> 22:57.000
Darling, heading toward a twisted signpost

22:57.084 --> 22:59.503
Heart fluttering, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

22:59.586 --> 23:02.339
Just the two of us, consolation prize

23:12.599 --> 23:14.726
Ah, the scent of dance

23:14.810 --> 23:16.561
I'm completely obsessed

23:16.645 --> 23:17.979
with you as you flutter down

23:18.063 --> 23:20.232
Ah, something smells off

23:20.315 --> 23:22.442
I'm blown away by you

23:22.526 --> 23:23.443
Bye-bye, mwah!

23:23.527 --> 23:26.571
It seems like I'm only good at

23:26.655 --> 23:29.324
workbooks for a child

23:29.407 --> 23:32.160
I want us to share even our growing pains

23:32.244 --> 23:34.913
No! No! Love's in gridlock!

23:35.122 --> 23:37.624
Forever and ever, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

23:37.707 --> 23:40.710
Darling, heading toward
a stagnant signpost

23:40.794 --> 23:43.296
Heart fluttering, I love you,
Shake Na Baby

23:43.380 --> 23:46.133
Singing a grand chorus cheekily

23:47.592 --> 23:49.636
- What the heck is-
- Escape is super impossible.

23:49.719 --> 23:52.347
- Hang on tight!
- I've never been in better condition.

23:52.430 --> 23:54.266
- That's water-absorbent polymers.
- I'll super enjoy this.

23:54.599 --> 23:56.977
Next time: "Lord Chladni."
